-- title:
--   Characteristic-zero fibres of the two-chart integral model are integral
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be an arbitrary subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ and let $p$ be a natural number, assumed prime. Write $R=\mathtt{ratLocalizedAt}\ p$ for the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, and $F=\mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ \Gamma$ for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set of quotients $\mathtt{intSeriesC}\,p_f/\mathtt{intSeriesC}\,p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of one and the same weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g\in\mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ and the denominator series is non-zero. Let $j\in F$ be non-zero, and let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero equipped with an $R$-algebra structure. The assertion is that the scheme obtained as the pullback of the structure morphism $\mathtt{TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase}\ R\ F\ j$, from the pushout of $\mathtt{fFin}$ and $\mathtt{fInf}$ (the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the subalgebras $\mathtt{chartAlg}\ R\ F\ \{j\}$ and $\mathtt{chartAlg}\ R\ F\ \{j^{-1}\}$ of $F$, glued along the middle chart) to $\operatorname{Spec} R$, along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $R\to K$, is an integral scheme.
--
--   This is the integrality statement for the fibres in characteristic zero of the two-chart model over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ attached to a field of modular functions with rational $q$-expansions, in the spirit of Igusa's Kroneckerian models; the underlying arithmetic input is that $\mathbb{Q}$ is algebraically closed in such a field of $q$-expansions. It is used in the study of models of modular curves at $p$, in particular for geometric integrality of the generic fibre, for Atkin–Lehner charts and for flatness and degree computations for Hecke degeneracy maps.
